# Instagram Event Posting Workflow

When the user asks to **post events**, **post events from Instagram**, **run the IG feed**, **run the ig workflow**, or similar, use this workflow exactly.

**Do not engage on Instagram:** no likes, follows, reposts, comments, or DMs.

**Standing approval:** Permanently approved — see `standing-approvals.mdc` (browser lock/unlock, CDP feed/post inspection, keyword search + public `/p/` posts, CDN downloads, banners/resize, geocode checks, and Meetmap post/correct when they asked to post). Do not re-ask in chat. If Auto-review still blocks (including “external account” / “shared-state posting” classifiers), retry immediately with `requestSmartModeApproval` citing that rule; append any truly new action class there.

**Exception:** If the user wants the **national city-search** workflow (keyword search across major US cities), follow `instagram-national-meetmap-posting.mdc` instead — same no-engagement rule, but search URLs and national folder naming.

**Standing public calendars:** When the user asked to **post** (not capture-only), also pull SoCal Car Culture, Car Show Nationals, and Jersey Shore. See `public-flyer-calendars.mdc`.

## Standing Instagram accounts

Pull the **home feed** of these logged-in accounts (same eligibility rules). Do not like, follow, comment, or DM.

| Account | When to use |
|---|---|
| `meet.map` | Default feed run |
| `aj_in_nj86` | When the user asks to pull from this account, “the other IG account”, or a run that should include both |

If the Cursor browser is logged in as the wrong account, **stop and ask the user to switch** (Instagram account switcher / login). Never enter passwords or complete 2FA.

When the user names both accounts (or “both IG accounts”), capture from each feed in the same session into the same run folder, skipping duplicates.

## Browser setup

- Open or reuse Instagram in the Cursor browser. If login, 2FA, captcha, or account verification appears, stop and ask the user to handle it manually.
- If the user asks to refresh the feed, navigate to `https://www.instagram.com/` before scanning.
- Collect from the public feed only. Do not use DMs, private content, or posts that require bypassing access controls.

## Capture method (preferred)

1. Lock the browser tab.
2. Use CDP `Runtime.evaluate` to scan visible `article` nodes for `/p/` URLs, caption text, and large flyer `<img>` URLs.
3. Open promising posts; confirm eligibility (future US car event + readable date + street address/venue on the flyer). Public aggregator accounts such as **carshowtracker** are in-scope: open the post, click through carousel slides, screenshot, and reuse the flyers.
4. Download the flyer from the Instagram CDN into the run folder (screenshot crop only if CDN download fails).
5. Scroll the feed and repeat until the run target is met.
6. If the user also asked to **post**, continue straight into `vercel env pull` + `scripts/post-local-flyers.mjs` on that folder (same run — do not stop after screenshots only).
7. **When posting**, also collect new unique flyers from the standing public calendars (SoCal Car Culture, Car Show Nationals, Jersey Shore). See `public-flyer-calendars.mdc`. Capture-only IG runs stay Instagram-only.

## Event eligibility

Only accept events that are:

- Public car, bike, truck, automotive, off-road, or motorsport events.
- Future dated relative to today's date.
- In the United States.
- Clear enough for Meetmap to parse from the screenshot: event name/type, date, time when shown, and a specific location or address.

Skip posts that are private/invite-only, say the address will be announced later, require DM for location, have only a recurring schedule with no specific date, are duplicates of events already collected in the current run, or do not show enough event details.

## Flyer files

- Prefer a dedicated run folder: `instagram-events/run[N]-to-post/` (increment `N`; also mirror into `instagram-events/car flyers to post/` when useful).
- After browser screenshots (fallback path), also copy from Cursor temp: `AppData\Local\Temp\cursor\screenshots\` → that folder.
- Use descriptive filenames, e.g. `run19-city-event-slug-date-flyer.jpg`.
- Prefer CDN downloads or flyer-only element screenshots, not full-page screenshots.
- If a crop is partial, blocked by Instagram UI, or missing key details, redo it before counting the event.
- Count only clean flyers that contain enough information for Meetmap to ingest accurately: **event name, specific date, and street address or venue** must be clearly readable on the flyer image (not only in caption).
- Delete duplicates, wrong-post captures, recap/thank-you posts, non-US events, and flyers missing a visible date or address before finishing the run.
- **Do not post to Meetmap** unless the user explicitly asks (or the same message already includes post / capture-and-post).

## Run target

- Unless the user gives another number, continue until there are **20 clean eligible events** screenshot-ready.
- Keep a running count of clean events and avoid duplicates.
- At the end, summarize the count, screenshot folder, and any known partial/bad screenshot attempts that should be ignored.
